1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,300
SEBI issues one circular — and within a week,

2
00:00:04,300 --> 00:00:07,400
every broker in the country is reading

3
00:00:07,400 --> 00:00:10,800
that same rule a little differently.

4
00:00:12,300 --> 00:00:15,100
The fix was never at the broker's end —

5
00:00:15,100 --> 00:00:17,500
a rule should be understood once,

6
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:19,900
at the source. So I built it.

7
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:23,200
This is Setu — a compiler for regulation.

8
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:25,900
This is the regulator's console;

9
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:27,950
the way SEBI would actually use it.

10
00:00:28,600 --> 00:00:31,400
It starts by ingesting every circular —

11
00:00:31,400 --> 00:00:34,300
each one is just a plain PDF.

12
00:00:34,300 --> 00:00:37,600
Setu splits it into its clause tree;

13
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:41,100
then, clause by clause, the language becomes

14
00:00:41,100 --> 00:00:44,000
rules a computer can actually check.

15
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:47,300
Here — “Periodic KYC updates every 2 years”

16
00:00:47,300 --> 00:00:50,600
becomes: last_updated + 730 days < TODAY.

17
00:00:50,600 --> 00:00:53,300
Each rule carries a confidence score —

18
00:00:53,300 --> 00:00:56,000
15 auto-approved, 2 flagged for review.

19
00:00:56,600 --> 00:00:59,600
Every rule takes its place on the graph —

20
00:00:59,600 --> 00:01:02,700
one canonical rule-graph, one source of truth.

21
00:01:02,700 --> 00:01:05,600
17 obligations, grouped by area — here, KYC.

22
00:01:05,600 --> 00:01:07,900
Click any node and you get proof:

23
00:01:08,400 --> 00:01:11,500
the original SEBI wording, highlighted,

24
00:01:11,500 --> 00:01:14,700
beside the executable rule and its confidence —

25
00:01:14,700 --> 00:01:17,900
days since last refresh, under 730.

26
00:01:18,600 --> 00:01:21,500
Now a new circular arrives — detected instantly.

27
00:01:21,500 --> 00:01:24,600
Setu reads it against the graph

28
00:01:24,600 --> 00:01:27,700
and works out what actually changed.

29
00:01:27,700 --> 00:01:31,000
Incident reporting: six hours becomes two.

30
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:34,200
Old rule left, proposed rule right.

31
00:01:34,200 --> 00:01:37,600
Impact, previewed before anything goes live:

32
00:01:37,600 --> 00:01:40,900
128 of 237 entities would be affected.

33
00:01:40,900 --> 00:01:44,500
One officer proposes; the approver signs off.

34
00:01:44,500 --> 00:01:47,800
Approved — committed and hash-chained, forever auditable.

35
00:01:48,400 --> 00:01:51,200
The other door: any intermediary just registers.

36
00:01:51,200 --> 00:01:54,300
Sharma Securities — category, profile, exchanges. Done.

37
00:01:54,300 --> 00:01:57,800
17 obligations map to them — live.

38
00:01:58,500 --> 00:02:01,300
Instantly: their own compliance dashboard —

39
00:02:01,300 --> 00:02:04,200
only the rules that apply to them.

40
00:02:04,200 --> 00:02:07,200
A fresh SEBI amendment is already here:

41
00:02:07,200 --> 00:02:10,300
the QSB cyber-audit cycle — cut to 90 days.

42
00:02:10,300 --> 00:02:12,900
101 days on the clock: red for Sharma.

43
00:02:13,600 --> 00:02:16,700
Step back — here's what Setu really is.

44
00:02:16,700 --> 00:02:20,400
One: self-healing compliance. Change a rule,

45
00:02:20,400 --> 00:02:23,600
and every obligation re-evaluates itself.

46
00:02:23,600 --> 00:02:27,100
Two: AI drafts. Humans approve. Always.

47
00:02:27,100 --> 00:02:30,300
Three: issued once — live everywhere, instantly.

48
00:02:30,300 --> 00:02:32,900
Four: every decision, fully traceable.

49
00:02:33,600 --> 00:02:36,600
The payoff: SEBI's rule-book, always current,

50
00:02:36,600 --> 00:02:39,600
with live oversight of every breach.

51
00:02:39,600 --> 00:02:42,700
Firms get a portal that does the work —

52
00:02:42,700 --> 00:02:44,900
no spreadsheets, no re-entry.

53
00:02:44,900 --> 00:02:47,800
Circular to firm-wide rollout: weeks to minutes.

54
00:02:48,600 --> 00:02:51,900
One graph. Issued once. Understood identically.

55
00:02:51,900 --> 00:02:54,800
The rule-book stops being a document you read

56
00:02:54,800 --> 00:02:58,200
and becomes a system that runs.
